Input: {"question": "What is the format of the film about the Donner Party?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d00", "start": 0, "end": 342, "text": "The Donner Party (1992 film) The Donner Party is a 1992 documentary film that traces the history of the Donner Party, an ill-fated pioneer group that trekked from Springfield, Illinois to Sutter's Fort, California - a disastrous journey of 2500 miles made famous by the tales of cannibalism the survivors told upon reaching their destination."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d00", "start": 343, "end": 535, "text": "The film, narrated by David McCullough, premiered at the Telluride Mountainfilm Festival in May 1992 with an introductory lecture on the Donner Party by noted Western historian David Lavender."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d00", "start": 536, "end": 627, "text": "It subsequently aired on PBS as part of the \"American Experience\" program in October, 1992."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d00", "start": 628, "end": 631, "text": "The"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d01", "start": 0, "end": 70, "text": "Troublesome Creek : A Midwestern Truman Two Days in October Ulysses S."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d01", "start": 71, "end": 276, "text": "Grant Vietnam : A Television History Walt Disney We Shall Remain Wild by Law Woodrow Wilson and the Birth of the American Century The Wright Stuff Retrieved from `` https : //en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php ?"}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d01", "start": 277, "end": 713, "text": "title=The_Donner_Party_ ( 1992_film ) & oldid=1244241936 `` Categories : 1992 films American Experience Television series by WNET American documentary films Films directed by Ric Burns 1992 documentary films